WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Bangladesh is a low-lying delta
country on the Bay of Bengal.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.990
A World Bank study found a ten-year
cyclone would flood 8 million people over

3
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.730
3 metres deep.

4
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.030
By 2050, a projected 22.5 million.

5
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:19.590
Bangladesh guards its coast with
6,000 kilometres of earth banks,

6
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.710
enclosing 139 polders.

7
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:28.130
Now, 700 hectares of trees have been
planted on their slopes and foreshores.

8
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.030
Why plant a forest in front of the banks?

9
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.170
Have they failed?

10
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.650
Is it for timber?

11
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.390
In this mission, you'll compare hard,
soft and ecosystem-based ways to defend

12
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.590
a coast.

13
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.370
Then you'll judge whether a
World Bank project here worked.

14
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.050
Your mission: explain why Bangladesh is
planting trees on the sea side of its

15
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:48.770
banks.
